  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Compounds which are more acidic then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas on reaction with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaHCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;Compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> i.e. Benzoic acid and compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e. picric acid both are more acidic than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8b19ac82-5b07-4e33-885d-bef75c91ae56-image.png\" style=\"width: 404px; height: 188px;\" /></p><p>equilibrium favours forward direction and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8593;</mo></math> is liberated.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a36c1468-d58f-4cf3-ad64-d53745bec0f5-image.png\" style=\"width: 468px; height: 202px;\" /></p><p>Equilibrium favours backward&nbsp;direction and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8593;</mo></math> is not liberated.</p>",
